    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d55">

                <pb facs="0167" n="65" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg65"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 2413/136–137.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chinese
                        Minister.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-05-29"><hi rendition="#italic">May 29,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 113.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith copy
                    of an act of Congress, approved May 25, 1908,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d55-f1"/>
                    whereby the President is authorized to return to the Chinese Government a
                    designated portion of the <pb facs="0168" n="66" xml:id="pg66"/> indemnity paid
                    by your Government in consideration of losses sustained by reason of the Boxer
                    disturbances of 1900.</p>
                <p>The Government of the United States would be glad to obtain from the Imperial
                    Chinese Government an expression of opinion as to the times and manner in which
                    the remission shall be made.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Bacon.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
